    prep: close review 95716 -- drop dangling base_root, fix two overclaiming comments
    
    - F1 (Consumption): ReleaseLocus.base_root was set by both constructors but read by no
      consumer. Deleted the field (and the locus.base assignment in the helper mint). base_root
      remains only as release_locus_record's local parameter, which is used to derive spine and
      the locus directory -- a real use, not a stored field.
    - F2 (Source annotations): removed the port comment's forward-reference to a "gate's
      leg_installed_paths" check that does not exist on this branch; the comment now states only
      what this diff actually establishes (dark_helper_snapshot_at installs the minted record, so
      the directory and the revision it names cannot diverge).
    - F3 (Epistemic humility): the helper-mint comment claimed board-function now mints once; the
      board-function converge / srv1 gpu-power-cap UNIT renderers and the attempt-system-unit launch
      still call helper_locus_dir directly for their own verify/display path (unrelated to the
      install port). Comment scoped to the root-helper snapshot INSTALL PORT only.
    
